// expect: 7
// A list pattern's element binders are declared at the element's width. A
// list's elements are words to the runtime, and a Float element's word is
// its address, so the pattern cashes the width where it binds. The binder
// was declared a word while the body read it as a float. Measured on boot
// 0bc8383e and 2d784560: did not assemble (`$a.f64` undefined), `mentl
// check` clean.
fn main() = match [1.5, 3.0] {
  [a, b] => if a + b > 4.0 { 7 } else { 1 },
}
